=== Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Skeletal muscle acts on bones through tendons. Tendons transmit force; ligaments instead join bones.]

#sol-item(2, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Cardiac muscle forms the muscular wall of the heart. Its contractions pump blood and are not usually under deliberate control.]

#sol-item(3, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Smooth muscle is found in walls of structures including the digestive tract. Its activity is generally involuntary and differs from skeletal muscle.]

#sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Skeletal muscle is generally voluntary but can also take part in reflexes and automatic adjustments. A reflex can activate skeletal muscle without a deliberate choice.]

#sol-item(5, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Cardiac muscle activity is generally involuntary. The heartbeat is not normally initiated by conscious commands.]

#sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Smooth muscle activity is generally involuntary. The movement of food through the gut illustrates involuntary muscular activity.]

#sol-item(7, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A tendon connects muscle to bone. Ligaments instead usually connect one bone to another.]

#sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A skeletal muscle pulls on a bone through a tendon. A muscle generates a pulling force rather than directly pushing a bone.]

#sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Antagonistic muscles contribute to opposing actions. The pair is a model of opposing actions, not a claim that no other muscles work.]

#sol-item(10, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[The biceps contributes to bending the elbow. Elbow flexion generally decreases the angle between the arm and forearm.]

#sol-item(11, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[The triceps contributes to straightening the elbow. Elbow extension generally increases the angle at the joint.]

#sol-item(12, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Elbow bending is flexion. Extension is the opposite movement in this simple comparison.]

#sol-item(13, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Elbow straightening is extension. Flexion is the opposite movement in this simple comparison.]

#sol-item(14, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Other muscles and co-activation can contribute to elbow movement and stability. Co-activation can support stability even when one action is the main focus.]

#sol-item(15, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Co-activation can help control and stabilise a joint. Stabilising a joint does not mean that opposing muscles must never contract together.]

#sol-item(16, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Isometric action produces force with little or no overall change in muscle length.]

#sol-item(17, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Holding a position can involve isometric muscle action.]

#sol-item(18, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Isometric action demonstrates force without appreciable shortening.]

#sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[The brain and spinal cord form the central nervous system.]

#sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Nerves carry signals between the central nervous system and other tissues.]

#sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Sensory information can help the nervous system respond.]

#sol-item(22, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Motor pathways carry signals involved in muscle activation.]

#sol-item(23, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A receptor detects a stimulus.]

#sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[An effector performs the response, such as muscle contraction.]

#sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A reflex involves a neural pathway producing a response.]

#sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A simple reflex model traces sensory information and a motor response.]

#sol-item(27, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Reflex pathways vary, and the brain may also process the event.]

#sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Movement depends on interacting body systems and surroundings.]

#sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Fatigue can alter performance and coordination.]

#sol-item(30, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Preparation can help but does not remove every hazard.]

#sol-item(31, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Progression should suit the person and context.]

#sol-item(32, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Concerning symptoms should be taken seriously and assessed appropriately.]

#sol-item(33, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Cardiac muscle is found in the heart wall.]

#sol-item(34, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A tendon connects muscle to bone and transmits force.]

#sol-item(35, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Ligaments connect bones and help stabilise joints.]

#sol-item(36, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A motor pathway carries signals to effectors such as muscles.]

#sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[The brain is part of the central nervous system.]

#sol-item(38, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[The spinal cord is part of the central nervous system.]

